# ComputerPruner — ignore rules
#
# Anything listed here is generated, machine-local, or secret. If a file is needed
# to BUILD the app from a clean clone, it must NOT appear in this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lockfiles — DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The instinct is to ignore lockfiles. Do not. `go.sum` and
# `frontend/package-lock.json` are supply-chain integrity controls: they pin the
# exact module/package versions and their checksums, which is what makes
# `go mod verify`, `npm ci`, govulncheck and reproducible release builds
# meaningful. CI installs from them (`npm ci` fails outright without one).
# Both MUST stay committed. Never add them below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only the compiled-output directory is ignored, never the whole build/ tree —
# build/appicon.png, build/darwin/*.plist and build/windows/* are Wails bundle
# inputs and are required to build.
#
# The negations below are documentation, not a safety net: they are no-ops today
# (nothing above them excludes those paths), and git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so they would NOT rescue the inputs if
# someone later broadened `build/bin/` to `build/`. Keep them as a marker of
# intent and do not rely on them.
build/bin/
!build/appicon.png
!build/darwin/
!build/windows/

# Compiled frontend bundle, regenerated by `wails build` / `vite build`.
# A local placeholder frontend/dist/index.html exists only to satisfy the
# //go:embed directive in main.go — do not delete it.
frontend/dist/

# GoReleaser output. Anchored with a leading slash so it only matches the
# repo-root dist/, not every nested directory that happens to be named "dist".
/dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
frontend/node_modules/
vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
# Anchored: an unanchored `*.out` would silently swallow any future
# internal/**/testdata/*.out golden file. Coverage output is listed explicitly
# below.
/*.out

# Coverage (CI writes coverage.out and uploads it as an artifact)
coverage.out
coverage.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wails generated code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `wails generate module` from the Go service structs. Never
# hand-edited, never committed.
frontend/bindings/
frontend/wailsjs/

# Hash Wails writes to detect frontend dependency changes between builds.
frontend/package.json.md5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment / secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tool config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-developer Claude Code overrides — machine-specific, and has leaked a
# personal path to a private dotfiles repo before. The rest of .claude/ (notably
# .claude/rules/) is shared project config and stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Release pipeline scratch (CI only)
#
# GoReleaser refuses to run against a dirty worktree, and the release workflow
# creates all three of these inside the checkout before invoking it:
#   artifacts/        raw per-matrix downloads from actions/download-artifact
#   dist-prebuilt/    the restaged layout .goreleaser.yaml's archives point at
#   release-notes.md  the body handed to --release-notes
# Leaving them untracked made `git status` non-empty and aborted the release
# after all three build jobs had already succeeded. Ignoring them is the fix.
artifacts/
dist-prebuilt/
release-notes.md
